DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T163000
UID:bistitchual-10336682017026@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a one session Cable Class. The class will 
 be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday November 7 from 2:30pm-4:30pm
  Have you been fantasizing about the cable sweater of your dreams? Take a 
 step towards making that dream a reality with our Cables Class and learn t
 he secrets of the deceptively simple yet hugely impactful cable knitting t
 echnique. In this class you will learn cable basics which will allow you t
 o tackle any cable project. Students will work through a small pattern tha
 t exemplifies cable techniques. Students should already be comfortable wit
 h the knit and purl stitches\, ribbing\, and pattern reading. Please bring
  worsted weight yarn and appropriate needles. If you need materials\, you 
 can purchase them in store with a 10% class discount. Cable needles will b
 e provided. Please note that classes will only proceed if we have a minimu
 m of two attendees . If the minimum is not met\, there will be the option 
 for a refund or to reschedule. There will be a four person maximum for eac
 h class. Please pre-book your spot to let us know you are coming! Cancella
 tion Policy Classes must be paid for at the time of registration to reserv
 e your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior to the start of the first
  class will be given a store credit. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs pr
 ior to the start of the class will not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/cable-class-november
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to Spin Your Own Yarn- November
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T140000
UID:bistitchual-10336668254466@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Spinning Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday November 7th
 \, 14\, 21st from 12:30pm - 2:00pm Learn how to transform fibre into yarn 
 with our drop spindle class! In this class you will learn how to use a dro
 p spindle to spin starting with woolly fibre and ending with a completed\,
  ready to use yarn. You will learn how to spin a single ply yarn\, how to 
 spin a 2-ply yarn using the Andean Plying method\, and how to chain ply fo
 r a 3-ply yarn over three classes. We will discuss spinning basics as well
  as different types of yarn\, fibres\, processing tools\, and preparations
  and how these affect the finished yarn. Drop spindles must be brought by 
 students or purchased in store. 50g of fibre provided in two different col
 ours. Please note that classes will only proceed if we have a minimum of t
 wo attendees . If the minimum is not met\, there will be the option for a 
 refund or to reschedule. There will be a four person maximum for each clas
 s. Please pre-book your spot to let us know you are coming! Cancellation P
 olicy Classes must be paid for at the time of registration to reserve your
  spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior to the start of the first class
  will be given a store credit. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to
  the start of the class will not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/learn-to-spin-your-own-yarn-november
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Crochet - October
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261018T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261018T160000
UID:bistitchual-10320075227394@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a two session Beginner Crochet Course. The
  classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday October 18th and 
 25th from 2:30pm-4:00pm Learn the fundamentals of crochet in this two part
  class. We will be covering chaining and single crochet\, as well as doubl
 e and half-double crochets. Don’t know what any of that means? Great\, y
 ou’re in the right place! We’ll provide all the materials\, including 
 a simple pattern that teaches you common terms and instructions you’ll e
 ncounter in most crochet projects. We will also discuss how to choose the 
 appropriate yarn and hook for a project as well as where you can take your
  crafting after you master these basic techniques. There’s a lot to lear
 n\, and we’re excited to accompany your beginning in the wonderful craft
  of crochet! Materials are included! - 50g ball of worsted weight cotton i
 n your choice of colour - 6mm crochet hook Our class size is capped at 4 p
 eople\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. Mike will share l
 ots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. About the instruct
 or: Tired of disposing of clothes that were still perfectly wearable\, Mik
 e (he/him) started crafting mainly as a means of mending and repair. This 
 led him to knitting (and later crochet)\, which pretty much immediately be
 came one of his favourite tools of self-expression. Please note that class
 es will only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimu
 m is not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. The
 re will be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot
  to let us know you are coming! Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid f
 or at the time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs
  or more prior to the start of the first class will be given a store credi
 t. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will
  not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-crochet-october-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
